      "writtenOn": "2023-11-03T04:37:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Is the race only possible for the head/tail pages ?\n\nYes the race is only for pages shared with other transactions.\n\n\u003e Do I understand this correctly? \n\nYour thoughts about optimization and avoiding the race are the exact intention here. So you do understand this correctly.\n\nWe still need the acq/rel semantics because of highly unlikely compiler optimization: e.g. the `vm_insert_page()` needs to be guaranteed to be called before setting `page-\u003epage_ptr` so we use the memory barrier to avoid reordering.",
      "parentUuid": "3485c5ae_510e5a04",
      "revId": "cba0dd82a60df879b05f8887eacf6faf78ab002b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
